Keep every definition transparent and computable so downstream provers can reduce it; avoid axioms or opaque wrappers.

**IMPORTANT:** Do NOT include `#eval` statements in your implementation code. Implementation files should only contain definitions (`def`, `structure`, `inductive`, etc.), not test or evaluation code. #eval statements:
- Will fail to build if functions use `sorry` placeholders
- Indicate testing rather than defining
- Belong in test files, not implementation files
